## Project-specific Auditd watches
## Evaluating ATT&CK-Based Detection Engineering for Linux Systems
## Author: Jeffrey Ofuje Adegoke
##
## These watches supplement the Neo23x0 Auditd ruleset used in the
## experimental laboratory and support Wazuh rules 100021-100023.
##
## Deployment:
## Copy this file to /etc/audit/rules.d/detection-engineering.rules
## and load the rules with:
##   sudo augenrules --load
##
## Paths under /home/jeffrey reflect the evaluated laboratory.
## Replace these paths as appropriate when adapting the rules to
## another Linux environment.

## Command-history tampering (T1070.003) - supports Wazuh rule 100021
-w /root/.bash_history -p wa -k history_tamper
-w /home/jeffrey/.bash_history -p wa -k history_tamper

## SSH authorized_keys persistence (T1098.004) - supports Wazuh rule 100022
-w /root/.ssh/authorized_keys -p wa -k ssh_key_change
-w /home/jeffrey/.ssh/authorized_keys -p wa -k ssh_key_change

## Log tampering (T1070.002) - supports Wazuh rule 100023
-w /var/log/auth.log -p wa -k log_tamper
-w /var/log/wtmp -p wa -k log_tamper
-w /var/log/btmp -p wa -k log_tamper

## Evaluated limitation:
## /var/log/wtmp and /var/log/btmp were already watched under the
## "session" key by the deployed Neo23x0 ruleset. During testing,
## events for these paths continued to use the existing key despite
## the additional watches being loaded. Rule 100023 was therefore
## validated as reliably covering /var/log/auth.log only.
